# Your rule content

- You are prohibited from adding any guard clauses to code that would hide an exception. We want the code to blow up right then and there if it encounters a scenario other than what we are directly implementing.
- Here is an example of a prohibited guard clause: if not hasattr(field, 'depends_on_parent') or not field.depends_on_parent(). you are disallowed from masking bugs with code like hasattr(field, 'depends_on_parent')